<title>BELGIUM: Delhaize shares star in Brussels due Food Lion buy.</title>
<headline>Delhaize shares star in Brussels due Food Lion buy.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian retail group Delhaize jumped 2.3 percent to 1,785 francs in Brussels on Monday morning after news late last week its U.S. unit Food Lion was to buy Florida-based Kash n' Karry Food Stores.</p>
<p>The deal is valued at $341 million. Kash n' Karry shareholders will receive $26 per share in cash, and Food Lion will refinance $221 million of Kash n' Karry debt.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a good move but the impact on profit will be long term,&quot; said Generale Bank analyst Sandra Vandersmissen.</p>
<p>This was mainly due to Kash n' Karry's low margins. She raised her Delhaize earnings per share forecast for 1997 by three francs to 97.</p>
